<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title><![CDATA[Linklog]]></title><description><![CDATA[Linklog]]></description><link>https://github.com/mondain-dev/linklog</link><generator>RSS for Node</generator><lastBuildDate>Mon, 03 Mar 2025 10:20:59 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://mondain-dev.github.io/linklog/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title><![CDATA[A guy who doesn’t understand Paul Verhoeven]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gk-QkTHXAAAOFxS.jpg:large"></p><p>Schwalbe⚡️ (@realhumanschwab) on X</p><p>Verhoeven did *intend* to make a movie that said “war makes fascists of us all” but he failed on every level because he doesn’t understand fascism, war or how propaganda works. 1/</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/realhumanschwab/status/1895914253506527284">https://x.com/realhumanschwab/status/1895914253506527284</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/realhumanschwab/status/1895914253506527284</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/realhumanschwab/status/1895914253506527284</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Context is that which is scarce, AI edition]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1528128033038602240/cMlQKeTG_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Linus (@thesephist) on X</p><p>Hypothesis: information work is overwhelmingly bottlenecked on availability of high-signal context more than by correct inference over the context. If right, implies higher ROI-per-flop of context building over pure logical inference. h/t @anandnk24</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/thesephist/status/1895887696268288119?s=46">https://x.com/thesephist/status/1895887696268288119?s=46</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/thesephist/status/1895887696268288119?s=46</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/thesephist/status/1895887696268288119?s=46</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[the most rapid change in human communication ever]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gk90PjWW4AA-Sam.jpg:large"></p><p>Ethan Mollick (@emollick) on X</p><p>The past 18 months have seen the most rapid change in human written communication ever By. September 2024, 18% of financial consumer complaints, 24% of press releases, 15% of job postings &amp; 14% of UN press releases showed signs of LLM writing. And the method undercounts true use</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/emollick/status/1895861786743881867?s=46&t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag">https://x.com/emollick/status/1895861786743881867?s=46&t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/emollick/status/1895861786743881867?s=46&amp;t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/emollick/status/1895861786743881867?s=46&amp;t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[the power of DeepSeek?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1225476100547063809/53jSWs7z_200x200.jpg"></p><p>Jeffrey Emanuel (@doodlestein) on X</p><p>OK, so now we know just how much more efficient DeepSeek is for inference in terms of total tokens per second processed. They are doing roughly 7-8x more tokens per second on an H-800 (a crippled, export-control version on the H-100) than the open-source state of the art on H-100</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/doodlestein/status/1895825001687011580?s=46">https://x.com/doodlestein/status/1895825001687011580?s=46</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/doodlestein/status/1895825001687011580?s=46</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/doodlestein/status/1895825001687011580?s=46</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[“…]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0304407620302773">https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0304407620302773</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0304407620302773</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0304407620302773</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Partial liberation from maternal human capital is a significant reason why American became such a land of opportunity]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gk-zsAXXwAAm445.jpg:large"></p><p>Lukas Althoff (@AlthoffLukas) on X</p><p>How did the US become a land of opportunity? In a new paper, we show that the country’s pioneering role in mass education was key to its rise in intergenerational mobility from 1850 to 1950. “America’s Rise in Human Capital Mobility”
with Harriet Brookes Gray &amp; @ReichardtHugo</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/AlthoffLukas/status/1895931540032667768">https://x.com/AlthoffLukas/status/1895931540032667768</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/AlthoffLukas/status/1895931540032667768</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/AlthoffLukas/status/1895931540032667768</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[Will Starfleet Academy become real in SF?]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/Gk_kCqxWEAA3iwD.jpg:large"></p><p>Crémieux (@cremieuxrecueil) on X</p><p>I love this. It’s a proposal to make Starfleet Academy real. The Space Force needs its academy. Full support.</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/cremieuxrecueil/status/1895984705176289392">https://x.com/cremieuxrecueil/status/1895984705176289392</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/cremieuxrecueil/status/1895984705176289392</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/cremieuxrecueil/status/1895984705176289392</guid><pubDate>Sun, 02 Mar 2025 16:55:32 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[A useful guide to “How Poverty Fell.”]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://justismills.substack.com/p/journal-club-how-poverty-fell">https://justismills.substack.com/p/journal-club-how-poverty-fell</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/03/sunday-assorted-links-506.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=sunday-assorted-links-506">Sunday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://j